While the computer is in tablet mode every panel is on automatic hide, and each goes back to the person's own
setting when tablet mode ends (ORDER 567; Daniel, 2026-11-14: "when in tablet mode only, can we make the taskbar
autohide?"). The shell follows KWin's org.kde.KWin.TabletModeManager. A panel keeps the visibility mode in force
apart from the person's own choice: the choice is the one that is saved and the one scripting reads, nothing is
written for tablet mode, and a panel already on automatic hide stays so
(plasma-workspace-panels-hide-in-tablet-mode.patch).

On unless plasmarc says [TabletMode] HidePanels=false, the switch of General Behavior in plasma-desktop
4:6.7.4-1+stereo3d4. A computer without a tablet mode, or a compositor that does not answer, changes nothing.
